WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:07.480
Speaker 1: We start today with some extraordinarily
sad audio that has been released of a conversation

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.130
with Democratic Senator Dianne Feinstein.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:17.580
This is a really tough story to do because
this is not an age just program in principle.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.310
And this is not about ageism.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.510
This is about competency.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:30.750
And it appears as though Senator Dianne Feinstein,
back from three months out of the Senate due

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:36.700
to health issues, has no memory of having
been gone for the last three months.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.640
Calls for her to resign are surging again.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:48.750
And we have to be able to you know, on the
one hand, we have empathy for Dianne Feinstein

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:53.030
and her family and as people, of course.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:56.649
And we also recognize that.

00:00:56.649 --> 00:01:01.090
It is not clear Dianne Feinstein is currently
fit to serve in the United States Senate.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.870
Now, for those of you who will write in and
say, David, Trump wasn't fit to serve and

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.330
he was president for four years.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.299
That's not really what this is about.

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:12.500
So we're going to play some audio.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.570
There were reports of this conversation.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.510
We now have the audio.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:23.880
Senator Dianne Feinstein, back from an absence
of several months while battling shingles,

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:28.870
is interviewed by Benjamin Arrakis of the
Los Angeles Times.

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:33.590
And she appears to have no memory whatsoever
of having been away for those three months.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.460
I mean, how you're feeling.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.700
Speaker 2: Since you are hearing.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.700
Fine.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.700
Yeah.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:40.700
The problem is the leg.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.700
The leg?

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:42.700
Yeah.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.700
What's wrong with you?

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.700
Well, no, nothing.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:45.930
Nothing saddening or just concern.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:46.930
Okay.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:47.930
But why?

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:51.189
Speaker 3: What is the response from your
colleagues being like, what is the well-wishes?

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:52.189
What have you heard?

00:01:52.189 --> 00:01:53.189
Speaker 4: What have I heard about what?

00:01:53.189 --> 00:01:54.439
Speaker 2: About your return?

00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:56.729
How have they felt about, you know.

00:01:56.729 --> 00:01:58.110
Speaker 4: Having been gone?

00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:59.110
Okay.

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:00.500
You should follow.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.289
Speaker 2: Me.

00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:03.660
I haven't been going.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:04.660
I've been working.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:12.629
You've been working from home, is what you're
saying?

00:02:12.629 --> 00:02:18.330
Oh, I've been here.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:22.609
I've been voting.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:23.609
So please either.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:24.609
Speaker 4: Know or don't know.

00:02:24.609 --> 00:02:25.609
Speaker 2: What do you say to Californians?

00:02:25.609 --> 00:02:26.609
Like real conversation resigned.

00:02:26.609 --> 00:02:29.739
Speaker 1: So at that point, Feinstein whisked
away.

00:02:29.739 --> 00:02:36.239
Democratic Congressman Ro Khanna again repeats
his call for Dianne Feinstein to resign after

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:37.550
this incident.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:38.550
S.F.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.580
Datacom reporting.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:45.250
Ro Khanna was the first member of Congress
to call for Feinstein's resignation, and he

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:51.810
is echoing that call a day after reporters
had this encounter where she appeared to not

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.989
remember that she had been absent for three
months.

00:02:54.989 --> 00:02:59.630
This is a really tough situation and it's
it's getting ugly and there really aren't

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:00.720
great options.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:06.959
And the best option that many are talking
about is that it is Feinstein's family who

00:03:06.959 --> 00:03:08.900
should convince her to resign.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:13.790
Gavin Newsom, the governor of California,
would get to select a replacement.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.269
And I don't remember based on it's in California.

00:03:16.269 --> 00:03:20.090
Whether there is or isn't a special election
depends on the number of days until the next

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:21.090
election.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.530
I believe because it's more than six months
until the 2024 election, there would be a

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:28.629
special election, I think, although I may
be wrong, will double check that.

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:35.709
But if it is not the options, according to
the U.S. Constitution, for removing a senator

00:03:35.709 --> 00:03:39.090
from office are expulsion or resignation.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.599
And expulsion would be a formal vote with
two thirds of the members of the Senate present

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:48.090
and voting in favor of of removal.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.890
Resignation is, of course, voluntary.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:51.739
It doesn't require a vote.

00:03:51.739 --> 00:03:53.640
It's just up to the senator.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.349
And there is no provision for a recall.

00:03:56.349 --> 00:03:58.300
This is a really sad and tough situation.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:03.489
And as I've said before, Dianne Feinstein
has an incredibly storied career in the Senate.

00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:08.450
She is the longest serving Democratic member
of the Senate right now, and I believe the

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:12.349
oldest by by a few months older than Chuck
Grassley.

00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:16.299
She'll be 90 in a few weeks.

00:04:16.299 --> 00:04:20.199
And this has been going on for years is the
truth.

00:04:20.199 --> 00:04:21.199
Okay.

00:04:21.199 --> 00:04:24.250
And at some point you have to just say this
is what it is.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:30.870
Dianne Feinstein reportedly regularly doesn't
remember meeting people that she sees regularly

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.780
and works with regularly.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:36.630
There are all of these examples of Dianne
Feinstein at Senate hearings where she will

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.370
read a question off of a piece of paper.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:43.251
It's not super clear if she totally gets the
question, but after the witness answers, she

00:04:43.251 --> 00:04:46.610
asks the exact same question a second time.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.120
This isn't serving anyone.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.620
This isn't serving democracy.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:55.460
This isn't serving the Democratic Party who's
had judicial nominations from Joe Biden held

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:57.290
up because of Feinstein's absence.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.130
She's on the Judiciary Committee.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:04.710
So at the end of the day, I don't know what
the mechanism is here, but we have to be able

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:07.790
to look at a situation and assess it for what
it is.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:11.039
Now, people have been writing to me saying,
David, there should be an upper limit on age

00:05:11.039 --> 00:05:15.750
for senators or an upper limit on the number
of years you're allowed to serve or whatever.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.830
Listen, maybe, maybe those things can all
be explored.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:23.330
Where we are right now is that this is the
situation and growing.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:26.060
Calls for Feinstein to resign.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:31.159
The audio is troubling and it's sad and it's
where we are right now

